    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0274" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/565</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-29T21:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 29, 1917, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 3, 11.40
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1823. Quiet to-day but Minister for Foreign Affairs says Bolsheviks circularizing
                    workmen and Bolshevik soldiers directing delegations be sent to conference and
                    protest against counter-revolutionary sentiment which seems prevailing there.
                    This may produce clash as workmen have [not] returned arms as commanded but
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs says Government confident can suppress outbreak and
                    such is also feeling of Minister of War who lunched at the Embassy to-day.
                    Cabled you <hi rendition="#italic">en chair</hi> placarded notice of protest
                    meeting to-morrow evening concerning America’s treatment of Alexander
                        Berkman of which I have notified Foreign Office. Notice unsigned
                    being evidently work of Bolsheviks. Cable immediately about Berkman’s crime and
                    prosecution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
